From de14bd95dfa85a3ab9482afb5142315837b298bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stepan Mazurov <smazurov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:18:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] uboot-airoha: reserve a recovery volume on the Gemtek
 W1700K

sysupgrade creates rootfs_data with all the space left in UBI, so a
recovery volume can only be added before the first sysupgrade, or by
removing rootfs_data. The UBI installer sized it to its own recovery
image, 91 LEBs (11,554,816 bytes), which a current recovery image no
longer fits into: a snapshot build is 11,658,164 bytes without padding,
and a release build also includes LuCI.

Create a 32 MiB recovery volume together with the other volumes when
the chainloader sets up UBI, before sysupgrade gives the rest to
rootfs_data. This costs 8% of the 390 MiB rootfs_data and leaves room
for the recovery image to grow. The volume starts out empty, which
boot_recovery treats like a missing one (bootm fails on the erased
data) and falls back to TFTP. The recovery image can be written to it
from the recovery or the production system:

  ubiupdatevol /dev/ubi0_N openwrt-airoha-an7581-gemtek_w1700k-ubi-initramfs-recovery.itb

where ubi0_N is the volume named "recovery" (ubinfo -a). Once written,
holding the reset button is no longer needed to recover from a broken
production volume.

Devices installed with the UBI installer already have a recovery volume
and are left as they are.

Signed-off-by: Stepan Mazurov <smazurov@gmail.com>
---
 package/boot/uboot-airoha/patches/404-add-gemtek-w1700k.patch | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/boot/uboot-airoha/patches/404-add-gemtek-w1700k.patch b/package/boot/uboot-airoha/patches/404-add-gemtek-w1700k.patch
index 3111aea..311ebaa 100644
--- a/package/boot/uboot-airoha/patches/404-add-gemtek-w1700k.patch
+++ b/package/boot/uboot-airoha/patches/404-add-gemtek-w1700k.patch
@@ -185,7 +185,7 @@ Signed-off-by: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
 +ubi_read_recovery=ubi check recovery && ubi read $initaddr recovery
 +ubi_prepare=ubi part ubi || run ubi_format ; run ubi_create_vols ; env exists _init_env && run _init_env
 +ubi_format=ubi detach ; mtd erase ubi && ubi part ubi ; reset
-+ubi_create_vols=ubi check ubootenv || ubi create ubootenv 0x1f000 dynamic ; ubi check ubootenv2 || ubi create ubootenv2 0x1f000 dynamic ; ubi check factory || ubi create factory 0x10000 static
++ubi_create_vols=ubi check ubootenv || ubi create ubootenv 0x1f000 dynamic ; ubi check ubootenv2 || ubi create ubootenv2 0x1f000 dynamic ; ubi check factory || ubi create factory 0x10000 static ; ubi check recovery || ubi create recovery 0x2000000 dynamic
 +_init_env=setenv _init_env ; saveenv ; saveenv
 --- /dev/null
 +++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/airoha/an7581-w1700k-ubi.dts
